            NESTED LOOP is a loop inside another loop. It can be used to iterate over a collection of items or to perform a task a certain number of times for each item in the collection. 
             


             ex.
            outer loop incharge making the rows
            inner loop incharge making the columns


            Console.Write("enter number of rows: ");
            int rows = Convert.ToInt32(Console.ReadLine());

            Console.Write("enter number of columns: ");
            int columns = Convert.ToInt32(Console.ReadLine());

            Console.Write("what symbol do you want to use? ");
            string symbol = Console.ReadLine();

            for (int i = 0; i < rows; i++)
            { //this code is in charge of making the rows, 
                for (int j = 0; j < columns; j++)
                { //this code is in charge of making the columns, it will repeat the symbol for the number of columns specified
                    Console.Write(symbol); // this code will print the symbol specified by the user for the number of columns specified
                }
                Console.WriteLine();
            }

            //how does it work? the outer loop will run for the number of rows specified by the user, and for each iteration of the outer loop, the inner loop will run for the number of columns specified by the user. The inner loop will print the symbol specified by the user for the number of columns specified, and then the outer loop will print a new line to move to the next row. This process will repeat until all rows and columns have been printed.

